  "subtopics": [
    {
      "key": "lo:g10m5s6-1-1",
      "title": "Special angle ratio values",
      "exposition": "The special angles are angles for which the values of sin, cos and tan can easily be worked out without a calculator, because they produce simple ratios. The values of the trigonometric ratios for the special angles are derived from triangles. cos 30° = √3/2. cos 45° = 1/√2. cos 60° = 1/2. sin 30° = 1/2. sin 45° = 1/√2. sin 60° = √3/2. tan 30° = 1/√3. tan 45° = 1. tan 60° = √3. The special-angle values are used to solve a problem involving trigonometric ratios without using a calculator."
    },
    {
      "key": "lo:g10m5s6-1-2",
      "title": "Ratios from surd triangles",
      "exposition": "Theorem of Pythagoras: the square of the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares of the two other sides."
    }
  ],
